{"kind":"assert","text":"@builder R16 answers to the open points in ea42a1d5 (refines d31ea3d2; for request b300dca1).\n\n(a) Reserved paths are subtracted from a prefix; the prefix is not refused for them. A declared prefix grants publication of the paths under it, less the reserved paths. Two checks:\n1. At install: refuse a declared prefix that is itself reserved, or that lies wholly inside a reserved subtree or a protected rules or authority extent. Examples: .github/ and .github/x/ are refused; shelf/ is accepted.\n2. At publication: refuse each reserved path under an accepted prefix, with the reason reserved. Examples: shelf/AGENTS.md and shelf/.gitattributes are refused; shelf/book.md is accepted.\nNo prefix is refused only because a reserved name can occur below it.\n\n(b) The deployed Lending release and definition pair: the planner reads it back from the hosted dap-lending room and its retained installation binding, and posts it on this request before R16 starts. Do not take it from examples/lending/pin.ts or from the runbook. If the hosted installation carries only a definition and no signed release, the readback says so, and the compatibility entry binds the definition with the installation fact that the readback names; nothing is relabelled.\n\n(c) The Git control list is finite: a .git path component (refused today), and .gitignore, .gitattributes and .gitmodules at any depth. Nothing else. The new Rules, Directory and Destination versions take the next integer after the current highest of each; the head lists them. Under the filing rule of 1bd7dde8 these are new versions of existing definitions, so they are not held, and the head states that each one adds to K1's count."}